"use strict";
window.LC_CHUNKS=window.LC_CHUNKS||{};window.LC_CHUNKS["school_mathematics_en"]=window.LC_CHUNKS["school_mathematics_en"]||{};window.LC_CHUNKS["school_mathematics_en"][3]={"school_mathematics_en:M3-L1":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L1\">M3-L1 – Rational expressions and equations<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M3 – Expressions, equations and inequalities<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Lower secondary education · foundations<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prior knowledge:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=school_mathematics&amp;module=M1&amp;lesson=L2&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M1-L2<\/a>; <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=school_mathematics&amp;module=M1&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M1-L3<\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong>Context:<\/strong> Core mathematics extension, informed by\nBavaria’s LehrplanPLUS M8.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Learning objectives<\/h2>\n<p>After this lesson, you can determine the domain of a rational\nexpression, manipulate rational expressions without losing their\noriginal domain restrictions, and solve rational equations with a\nsubstitution check. You can recognise when an algebraic candidate is\ninvalid because it lies outside the domain.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Determine the domain before calculating<\/h2>\n<p>Here a rational expression is a quotient of two polynomials. The\nnumerator is above the fraction bar and the denominator is below. We\nwork over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℝ<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb R<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\n(the real numbers). Division by zero is undefined, so we exclude every\nzero of each original denominator. For example:<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>−<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"><\/mspace><mi>D<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℝ<\/mi><mo>\\<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}<\/mo><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T(x)=\\frac{x^2-4}{x-2},\\qquad D=\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{2\\}.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>The symbol\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>\\<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\setminus<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nmeans “excluding”, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>D<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ndenotes the domain. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\ne2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nfactor the numerator as\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(x-2)(x+2)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nCancelling gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T(x)=x+2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nbut only for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>∈<\/mo><mi>D<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\in D<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\n(read: x belongs to D). The simplified expression, treated as a separate\nfunction, has a larger domain than the original. The original graph has\na missing point at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(2,4)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\nthe restriction survives the simplification.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-school-mathematics-en/media/img/S_MAT_033_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Coordinate system: rising line with open circle at 2,4; horizontal line at y equals 3; filled intersection point at 1,3.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: The line\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=x+2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nwith a hole at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(2,4)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand comparison line\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nTheir intersection is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(1,3)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Operations with rational expressions<\/h2>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col class=\"lc-col-third\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-third\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-third\">\n<\/colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation<\/th>\n<th>Rule<\/th>\n<th>Condition<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Multiplying numerator and denominator<\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac ab=\\frac{ac}{bc}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b\\ne0,c\\ne0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cancelling<\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{ac}{bc}=\\frac ab<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b\\ne0,c\\ne0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Addition / subtraction<\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>±<\/mo><mfrac><mi>c<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><mo>±<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac ab\\pm\\frac cd=\\frac{ad\\pm bc}{bd}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>d<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b\\ne0,d\\ne0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Multiplication<\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>⋅<\/mo><mfrac><mi>c<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac ab\\cdot\\frac cd=\\frac{ac}{bd}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>d<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b\\ne0,d\\ne0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Division<\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>:<\/mo><mfrac><mi>c<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/mrow><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac ab:\\frac cd=\\frac{ad}{bc}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>d<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b\\ne0,d\\ne0,c\\ne0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>The letters represent numbers or expressions; with variables, the\nconditions must hold for each substitution. Only common factors may be\ncancelled, not individual terms in a sum. Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>/<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(x+3)/x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis not equal to 3 in general. A common denominator must be nonzero at\nevery permitted input.<\/p>\n<p>For example,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>2<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>+<\/mo><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/mfrac><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac1{x+1}=\\frac{3x+2}{x(x+1)}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nwhere\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\ne0,-1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nFor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>x<\/mi><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mo>:<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><mi>x<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{x}{x+1}:\\frac{x-2}{x}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nwe additionally require\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\ne2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nas well as\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\ne0,-1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe result\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mfrac><msup><mi>x<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/mfrac><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{x^2}{(x+1)(x-2)}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nmust retain the original restriction\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\ne0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Solving a rational equation<\/h2>\n<p>We want\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>−<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{x^2-4}{x-2}=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nFirst record\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℝ<\/mi><mo>\\<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D=\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{2\\}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nOn this set, multiplying both sides by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x-2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis reversible:<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>−<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><mspace width=\"1.0em\"><\/mspace><mo>⇔<\/mo><mspace width=\"1.0em\"><\/mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x^2-4=3x-6\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad(x-1)(x-2)=0.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>The candidates are 1 and 2. Only 1 belongs to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>D<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nCheck:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(1-4)/(1-2)=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe solution set is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L=\\{1\\}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe figure in S2 shows the same solution as an intersection; there is no\nfunction value at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nSolving the simplified equation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x+2=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nyields the same value directly, provided the domain is retained.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Application: combined flow rate<\/h2>\n<p>One pump fills a tank on its own in 6 hours. A second takes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nhours. With constant additive rates and a simultaneous start, both pumps\nfill the tank in 4 hours. One full tank is the unit; the filling rates\nare\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>6<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/6<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ntanks per hour. Therefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>6<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/6+1/x=1/4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>12<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/x=1/12<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>12<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=12<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe contextual restriction is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x&gt;0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nnot merely\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\ne0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nCheck:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>6<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>12<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/6+1/12=1/4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIf the pumps interact or their rates vary, this model need not\napply.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Self-assessment<\/h2>\n<h3 id=\"exercises\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises<\/h3>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Determine the domain of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msup><mi>x<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>−<\/mo><mn>9<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(x^2-9)/(x-3)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand simplify. Is the original expression defined at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Calculate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>+<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2/(x-1)+3/(x+1)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand state its domain.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Solve\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x/(x-2)=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand check by substitution.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Explain why\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msup><mi>x<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>−<\/mo><mn>9<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(x^2-9)/(x-3)=6<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nhas no solution.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">One machine completes a job in 10 hours; two together take 4 hours.\nFind the second machine’s individual time under the same assumptions as\nin S5.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<details class=\"lc-solutions\" data-lc-section=\"S6\"><summary>Show solutions<\/summary>\n<div>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℝ<\/mi><mo>\\<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D=\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{3\\}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nsimplified to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x+3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>D<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe value at 3 remains excluded.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℝ<\/mi><mo>\\<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D=\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{-1,1\\}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nresult\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msup><mi>x<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(5x-1)/(x^2-1)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\ne2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=3(x-2)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nCheck:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3/(3-2)=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">On\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>D<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x+3=6<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ngives the sole candidate 3. It is not permitted;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>⌀<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L=\\varnothing<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>4<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>10<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>20<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/x=1/4-1/10=3/20<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>20<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=20/3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nhours, or 6 hours 40 minutes. The two rates sum to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<\/div>\n<\/details>\n<h2 id=\"S7\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Connections and limitations<\/h2>\n<p>Review <a href=\"index.html?course=school_mathematics&amp;module=M1&amp;lesson=L2&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M1-L2<\/a> for fractions and\n<a href=\"index.html?course=school_mathematics&amp;module=M1&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M1-L3<\/a> for algebraic\ntransformations. <a href=\"index.html?course=school_mathematics&amp;module=M2&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M2-L1<\/a> examines\nfamilies of functions further. Rational inequalities also require\nanalysing the denominator’s sign; the rules for linear inequalities in\n<a href=\"index.html?course=school_mathematics&amp;module=M3&amp;lesson=L2&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M3-L2<\/a> are a prerequisite. This\nlesson is limited to equations and real inputs.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S8\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://de.serlo.org/mathe/156343/rechnen-mit-bruchtermen\">Serlo –\nRechnen mit Bruchtermen (Operations with rational expressions)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> ·\nSection 4, domain restrictions and their preservation; the source uses\nrational inputs, whereas this lesson explicitly uses real inputs · Last\naccessed: 2026-11-24 · Content verified: 2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://de.serlo.org/mathe/1851/bruchgleichungen-loesen\">Serlo –\nBruchgleichungen lösen (Solving rational equations)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Solving\nprocedure and exclusion of invalid candidates · Last accessed:\n2026-11-24 · Content verified: 2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","school_mathematics_en:M3-L2":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L2\">M3-L2 – Linear inequalities and intervals<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M3 – Expressions, equations and inequalities<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Lower secondary education · foundations<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prior knowledge:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=school_mathematics&amp;module=M1&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M1-L3<\/a>; <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=school_mathematics&amp;module=M1&amp;lesson=L8&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M1-L8<\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong>Context:<\/strong> Core mathematics extension, informed by\nBavaria’s LehrplanPLUS M8.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Learning objectives<\/h2>\n<p>You can solve linear inequalities and justify when the inequality\nsign reverses. You can represent solution sets as intervals and on\nnumber lines and restrict them to the appropriate number system in\napplied problems.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Comparison and solution sets<\/h2>\n<p>An equation requires equality, whereas an inequality compares\nquantities.\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a&lt;b<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nmeans “a is less than b”, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\le b<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nincludes equality;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>&gt;<\/mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">&gt;<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>≥<\/mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ge<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nexpress the reversed comparisons. A linear inequality in one variable\ncan be rearranged to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ax+b&lt;0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nor one of the other three comparison forms. The coefficients\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a,b<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nare fixed real numbers; in the special case\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe variable disappears. The solution set contains all real inputs that\nmake the comparison true.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Equivalent transformations<\/h2>\n<p>Adding the same number to both sides preserves the difference between\nthe values. Multiplying or dividing by a positive number also preserves\norder. A negative factor reverses the order: multiplying\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2&lt;5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nby\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-2&gt;-5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nDivision by zero is forbidden; multiplying by zero is not\nreversible.<\/p>\n<p>For example:<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>7<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mspace width=\"1.0em\"><\/mspace><mo>⇔<\/mo><mspace width=\"1.0em\"><\/mspace><mo>−<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>6<\/mn><mspace width=\"1.0em\"><\/mspace><mo>⇔<\/mo><mspace width=\"1.0em\"><\/mspace><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">7-3x\\le1\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad-3x\\le-6\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad x\\ge2.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>The first step subtracts 7 from both sides; the second divides by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand reverses the comparison. Check: at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\le1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-2\\le1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4\\le1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis false. These checks illustrate the result; the equivalent\ntransformations prove it for all real numbers.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Intervals and number lines<\/h2>\n<p>A square bracket includes a finite endpoint; a round parenthesis\nexcludes it.\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>∞<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis not a real number, so an infinite endpoint always uses a parenthesis.\nOn a number line a filled point is included and an open circle is\nexcluded.<\/p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Condition<\/th>\n<th>Interval<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\ge2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>∞<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[2,\\infty)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x&lt;2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mi>∞<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(-\\infty,2)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-1&lt;x\\le4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(-1,4]<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>all real numbers<\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mi>∞<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>∞<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(-\\infty,\\infty)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>no solution<\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>⌀<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varnothing<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-school-mathematics-en/media/img/S_MAT_034_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Two number lines: top extends right from 2 inclusive; bottom extends from minus 1 exclusive to 4 inclusive.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: The interval\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>∞<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[2,\\infty)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nwith an included endpoint and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(-1,4]<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nwith an excluded and an included endpoint.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Multiple conditions and special cases<\/h2>\n<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>9<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-1&lt;2x+1\\le9<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nboth conditions must hold. Subtract 1 everywhere and divide by 2:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-1&lt;x\\le4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe common solution set is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(-1,4]<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nFor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2x+1&lt;2x+5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nsubtracting\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nleaves the true statement\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1&lt;5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nso every real number is a solution. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2x+5&lt;2x+1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe remaining statement is false; there is no solution. These cases\nexplain why blindly dividing by a potentially zero coefficient is\ninvalid.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Application: a limited budget<\/h2>\n<p>An event venue charges a base fee of 30 euros plus 4 euros per\nperson. The budget is at most 78 euros. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\npeople,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>30<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>78<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">30+4n\\le78<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>12<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\le12<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe model variable is a nonnegative integer; the actual solution set is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>…<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mn>12<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\{0,1,\\dots,12\\}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nTwelve people cost 78 euros, thirteen cost 82 euros. A condition of\n“less than 78 euros” would exclude twelve. The result does not account\nfor extra fees or a minimum number of attendees.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S7\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Self-assessment<\/h2>\n<h3 id=\"exercises\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises<\/h3>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Solve\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>5<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mn>11<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">5-2x&gt;11<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand state the interval.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Solve\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>7<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-3\\le2x+1&lt;7<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand mark the endpoints.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Solve\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4(x+1)\\ge4x+4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4(x+1)&lt;4x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Renting a device costs 12 euros plus 2.50 euros per hour. The budget\nis strictly less than 32 euros. How many whole hours are possible?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Explain why\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>⋅<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>⋅<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\cdot a&lt;x\\cdot b<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ndoes not imply\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a&lt;b<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nin general.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<details class=\"lc-solutions\" data-lc-section=\"S7\"><summary>Show solutions<\/summary>\n<div>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-2x&gt;6<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x&lt;-3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\ninterval\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mi>∞<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(-\\infty,-3)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mn>4<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-4\\le2x&lt;6<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nhence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-2\\le x&lt;3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[-2,3)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nleft endpoint included, right excluded.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">The first reduces to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4<\/mn><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4\\ge4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℝ<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb R<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe second reduces to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4&lt;0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>⌀<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varnothing<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>12<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>2.5<\/mn><mi>h<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>32<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">12+2.5h&lt;32<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>8<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h&lt;8<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nWith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h<\/mi><mo>∈<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>…<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h\\in\\{0,1,2,\\dots\\}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n0 to 7 whole hours are possible, at most 7.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">When\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x&gt;0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nthe order stays the same; when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x&lt;0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nit reverses. When\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nthe initial strict inequality is false, and division would be invalid.\nExample:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=-1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b=2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mn>5<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-5&lt;-2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nbut\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>5<\/mn><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">5&gt;2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<\/div>\n<\/details>\n<h2 id=\"S8\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Connections and limitations<\/h2>\n<p><a href=\"index.html?course=school_mathematics&amp;module=M1&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M1-L3<\/a> supplies algebraic\ntransformations, and <a href=\"index.html?course=school_mathematics&amp;module=M1&amp;lesson=L8&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M1-L8<\/a> covers\nlinear functions. Graphically,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>g<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)\\le g(x)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ncorresponds to the region in which the graph of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis no higher than the graph of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>g<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nWith rational expressions from <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=school_mathematics&amp;module=M3&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M3-L1<\/a>, domain restrictions and\nchanging signs also matter. General rational or quadratic inequalities\nare not solved in this lesson.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S9\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://openstax.org/books/intermediate-algebra-2e/pages/2-5-solve-linear-inequalities\">OpenStax\n– Intermediate Algebra 2e, 2.5 Solve Linear Inequalities<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Interval\nnotation, negative factors and special cases · Last accessed: 2026-11-24\n· Content verified: 2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://de.serlo.org/mathe/82843/lineare-ungleichungen\">Serlo –\n(Lineare) Ungleichungen (Linear inequalities)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Reversing the\ninequality sign when multiplying or dividing by a negative number · Last\naccessed: 2026-11-24 · Content verified: 2026-11-24<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>"};
